<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">15 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 15 August, from 778 to 1947.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charlemagne.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">778 <span class="tih-ago">1,248 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Basques destroy Charlemagne's rearguard at Roncevaux</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Basque fighters ambushed Charlemagne's rearguard in the Pyrenees, killing the commander Roland. The Song of Roland later recast the skirmish as a heroic stand against Saracens.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basques">Basques</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/scotland" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scotland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1057 <span class="tih-ago">969 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Macbeth is killed at the Battle of Lumphanan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King Macbeth of Scotland was killed at Lumphanan in Aberdeenshire by forces of Malcolm Canmore, Duncan's son. He had ruled for 17 years and even made a pilgrimage to Rome.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1534 <span class="tih-ago">492 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ignatius of Loyola and companions take vows at Montmartre</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ignatius and six companions vowed poverty and chastity in a chapel on Montmartre in Paris. The group became the Society of Jesus, approved by the Pope in 1540.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1769 <span class="tih-ago">257 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon Bonaparte is born in Corsica</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Napoleone Buonaparte was born in Ajaccio, a year after France acquired Corsica from Genoa. He rose to become Emperor of the French and redrew the map and laws of Europe.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corsica">Corsica</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hirohito" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hirohito.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1945 <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Hirohito broadcasts Japan's surrender</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">For the first time, ordinary Japanese heard their emperor's voice as he announced acceptance of the Allied terms. The day is marked as VJ Day in Britain; the formal surrender was signed on 2 September.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hirohito">Hirohito</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pakistan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1947 <span class="tih-ago">79 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">India becomes independent as British rule ends</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At midnight India became independent, a day after Pakistan. Partition uprooted perhaps 15 million people and communal violence killed hundreds of thousands, possibly up to two million.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li></ol>
